-- RM-BS-QUNIVERSE-SMALL-1 slice 1 (CASCADE-SHADOW-1, 2026-11-05, charter pillar cost, program QNFO.OPS with QNFO.RSCH): roadmap_implementation 3257, blue-sky bet B1 (docs/BLUE-SKY-ROADMAP-2026-11.md).
-- WHAT WAS READ BEFORE BUILDING (2026-11-05, read-only): qnfo-ai had no scheduled handler (cloud_ops_events held no row of kind autorouter-shadow, migrations/2026-11-05-autorouter-eval-f4.sql), so a shadow
-- evaluation that nothing calls measures nothing; the A/B harness in qnfo-ai-calibration (model_ab_runs) only judges a model change that already happened (its last 12 rows: 9 error, 2 inconclusive, 1 pass);
-- ai_queries holds no organic stage prompts (its rows are the A/B harness's own fixtures), so a gold-labelled fixture set is the base of the eval.
-- WHAT WAS BUILT (qnfo-ai 5.48.0, PR 7689, merged 2026-11-05T04:15:26Z, deployed 04:15:49Z): a cron trigger (40 * * * *) and a scheduled handler; once per 22 hours the incumbent gpt-oss-120b and three cheaper
-- candidates answer 24 gold-labelled classification fixtures through the raw binding; label equality scores them; cloud_ops_events kind cascade-shadow (one row per candidate) and cascade-shadow-run (one per run)
-- carry accuracy, the paired difference, the noise floor (one standard error of the paired difference), the kill-rule verdict, measured neurons and the cost ratio. Shadow only: no stage is moved.
-- WHAT WAS READ AFTER THE DEPLOY (2026-11-05T04:43Z): GET /health version 5.48.0-codeagent; the Cloudflare schedules API lists cron 40 * * * * created 04:15:49Z; the first tick fired at 04:40:41Z and wrote
-- cascade-shadow-run 704303b30936 (status ok, 24 model calls, 10.3 s) and one cascade-shadow row. Two findings from that row, both filed below as CASCADE-SHADOW-1.1: (1) the run was lean because the 30-day spend
-- governor says downgrade (total 162.76 >= cap 60), which is the steady state, and lean kept only the first candidate (qwen3-30b-a3b-fp8), so the two candidates that are cheaper in practice (gpt-oss-20b, glm-5.3-flash)
-- were never asked; (2) a run of an older harness revision would block the gate for 22 hours after a fix, so the gate must count only runs of the current revision.
-- THIS FILE: sets row 3257 to partial with that evidence, registers the failure mode "the shadow stops running" with a detector contract, files slices 1.1 and 1.2 for the code loop, logs the decision.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = 'planned', verified_at = NULL, evidence = 'docs/BLUE-SKY-ROADMAP-2026-11.md' WHERE id = 3257 AND item = 'RM-BS-QUNIVERSE-SMALL-1'; UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = 'superseded', last_verdict = 'superseded:rollback' WHERE class = 'fm-cascade-shadow-silent'; UPDATE agent_issues SET status = 'closed' WHERE source = 'session:W2-H-3257' AND title LIKE 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.OPS CASCADE-SHADOW-1.%' AND status = 'open';
-- The Rollback leaves the failure_modes row and the decision row (decision_log is append-only), supersedes the detector and closes the filed issues; the worker change is a revert of the pull request.
-- CAUSE-MAPPED: registers no metric_registry row.

UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = 'partial', verified_at = datetime('now'),
  evidence = 'PARTIAL (W2-H, PR 7689, 2026-11-05): slice 1 of B1 is CASCADE-SHADOW-1 in qnfo-ai 5.48.0, merged 04:15:26Z and read live. /health answers 5.48.0-codeagent; the Cloudflare schedules API lists cron 40 * * * * (created 04:15:49Z; qnfo-ai had no scheduled handler before, which is why the Auto Router replay of RM-AUTOROUTER-EVAL-1 never ran). The first tick fired at 04:40:41Z and wrote cloud_ops_events cascade-shadow-run 704303b30936 (status ok, 24 model calls in 10.3 s) and one cascade-shadow row: qwen3-30b-a3b-fp8 against gpt-oss-120b is not_cheaper (accuracy 1.0 against 1.0 on 12 fixtures, noise floor 0.083, 113.1 against 108.7 neurons for the same fixtures, a measured saving of -4.1 percent: the cheap per-token model spends its saving on hidden thought, 229 completion tokens for a one-word answer in a direct API probe, 7.24 neurons against 6.39). Direct API probe of one fixture, usage.neurons: gpt-oss-120b 6.39, qwen3-30b-a3b-fp8 7.24, gpt-oss-20b 3.60, glm-5.3-flash 3.50, all answering correctly, so the rate table matches the meter and the two cheapest in practice are the two the lean run did not ask. How it works: once per 22 hours the incumbent gpt-oss-120b and three cheaper candidates answer 24 gold-labelled classification fixtures (severity triage, queue routing, degenerate-text pre-screen) through the raw binding, label equality scores them (no model judge), each candidate gets a row with accuracy, paired difference, noise floor (one standard error of the paired difference), verdict worse / eligible / not_cheaper / error and measured neurons. Shadow only, no stage moved; ops_config cascade_shadow = off stops it; at most 96 model calls a day, about 3k neurons. Open: (1) CASCADE-SHADOW-1.1 filed (lean runs keep every candidate, the gate counts only runs of the current harness revision, usage.neurons cross-check); (2) CASCADE-SHADOW-1.2 filed (a decision endpoint: three consecutive eligible runs promote, one worse run reverts); (3) the v0 fixtures are easy (every model scored 1.0 on the 12 asked), public in the repository and so not sealed against the code loop: harder, fleet-labelled fixtures from D1 are the slice after 1.2; (4) not started: Clef decision models, the Auto Router replay (caller in qnfo-cloud-ops, issue 1001898), GEPA, distillation, model aliases, reasoning effort per stage. Detector: fm-cascade-shadow-silent reads a finished run inside 26 hours.'
  WHERE id = 3257 AND item = 'RM-BS-QUNIVERSE-SMALL-1' AND status IN ('planned', 'in_progress');

